    "reasoning": "q-119132: Integration gives y=-2e^{-x/4}+C. Every solution is increasing and concave down, approaching y=C as x increases. Current option 2 shows this family and matches MA's labeled solution sketch; the different image paths identify equivalent unlabeled and labeled graphs. q-13817: f(1)=e^{-1}, f'(1)=-2e^{-1}, and f''(1)=2e^{-1}, giving option 3 by the Taylor formula. q-15490: f''(0)=-1/25, so the quadratic coefficient f''(0)/2 is -1/50, option 1. q-84716: The vertex and point (-4,4) give y^2=-4x. Option 1 generates the entire parabola because y=-2t and x=-t^2 with unrestricted real t. This agrees with the earlier answer and the current captured solution; the extra spacing in the choice has no mathematical effect. Each answer is supported by its own worked solution. No submitted grades are supplied.",
